 ('9702_w23_13_q14',[2],1,'Identify','Pressure is force per unit area, so A is correct. C is mass per unit volume, the definition of density.',{'B':'m2','C':'m2','D':'m2'}),
 ('9702_s21_12_q14',[2],4,'Calculate','The total weight is shared by four circular feet and $A=(C/2\\pi)^2\\pi$, giving about 85 kPa. A omits $g$; D forgets the four feet.',{'A':'m2','D':'m2'}),
 ('9702_w22_13_q15',[3],3,'Determine','For a cube, $p=mg/A=\\rho L^3g/L^2=\\rho gL$, so B is correct. C retains area instead of the height after dividing volume by area.',{'A':'m3','C':'m2','D':'m2'}),
 ('9702_w20_11_q14',[4],4,'Calculate','The gas side pushes the water lower, so $p_{\\mathrm{gas}}=p_{\\mathrm{atm}}+\\rho g(0.314-0.102)\\approx103$ kPa. C overlooks the full pressure rise after rounding.',{'A':'m4','B':'m4','C':'m4'}),
 ('9702_w19_13_q13',[4],5,'Determine','Density falls linearly from 1.3 to zero, so mean density is 0.65 kg m$^{-3}$; $h=p/(\\rho_{\\mathrm{mean}}g)\\approx16$ km. A uses sea-level density throughout.',{'A':'m4','C':'m4'}),
